    "methods_description": "Simultaneous EEG-ESG-ENG-EMG recordings were acquired from 40 participants under four conditions: resting state with eyes open, mixed median nerve stimulation (arm nerve), mixed tibial nerve stimulation (leg nerve), and alternating mixed median or tibial nerve stimulation. Recordings included electrocardiographic and respiratory signals. EEG channel Fz was referenced to both the right mastoid (standard EEG reference) and the 6th thoracic vertebra (ESG reference).",
